OL,3,GNEWSALibrary's first edition reveals
OL,4,AAusten's early fans
OL,5,
OL,6,FA first edition of Jane Austen's debut
OL,7,Fnovel has shed light on the author's
OL,8,Fconnection with one of Britain's
OL,9,Fhistoric country houses.
OL,11,FThe 1811 first edition of Sense and
OL,12,FSensibility is on the shelves at
OL,13,FLongleat House in Wiltshire, with its
OL,14,Ftitle page still carrying the anonymous
OL,15,Fattribution "By A Lady".
OL,17,FIt is thought to have been acquired by
OL,18,Fthe 2nd Marquess of Bath around the
OL,19,Ftime of its publication which
OL,20,Fhistorians say is evidence Austen was
OL,21,Fbeing read by the elite social class
OL,22,Fduring her lifetime.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
